{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"priceless-charred-fruitbat","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Operator-approved early removal (pre-1.0 breaking pass #3), 2026-08-12. Source: the DEPRECATION REMOVAL-READINESS SURVEY, comment #11 on childsafe-bizarre-lorikeet (b902-18af-14ed-4da1), Tier 2 item 2 — \"strongest candidate for the next breaking window\". Operator ruling (verbatim): \"The two best candidates and the one ready now are all approved for removal.\"\n\n## What\n\nRemove the three deprecated single-pass review PUBLIC entry points (story 316a, deprecated 31f352d535, shipped v0.11.0):\n\n- CLI verb `rebar review` — intercept `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:50,512-514` + handler `_review` at `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py:133-207`.\n- Library `rebar.llm.review_ticket` — the warn-and-delegate wrapper `src/rebar/llm/operations.py:135-183`, its `__all__` row at `:33`, and the re-export at `src/rebar/llm/__init__.py:54,119`.\n- MCP tool `review_ticket` — `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:60-95`.\n\nReplacements: `rebar review-plan` / `rebar.llm.review_plan` / the `review_plan` MCP tool.\n\n## What STAYS (do not touch)\n\nThe single-pass ENGINE `rebar.llm.operations._review_ticket_impl` (`src/rebar/llm/operations.py:185+`) STAYS — it has live internal consumers at `src/rebar/llm/review_workflows.py:86` and `src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py:348`. The third consumer (`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:92,95`) disappears with the MCP tool, taking it from 3 to 2. `src/rebar/schemas/review_result.schema.json` also STAYS — `review_result` is still produced by `review-code` and the workflow path.\n\n## Known hazards (found by inventory; each is a drift-gated set that must move in ONE commit)\n\n1. **CLI ladder parity** — `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py:74-79` (`INTERCEPT_COMMANDS[\"review\"]`), the intercept ladder in `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py`, and `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py:43` (`_LADDER`). The script self-checks its curated key set against the ladder at `gen_cli_reference.py:144-156`.\n2. **MCP manifest mirror** — the `REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_LLM` description string at `src/rebar/mcp_server.py:128-129` is mirrored verbatim into `server.json:33` and into generated `docs/mcp-reference.md:46,52,94` (gated by `scripts/check_server_manifest.py` + the mcp-reference drift gate).\n3. **Schema wiring** — `src/rebar/schemas/__init__.py` loses `\"review\": PLAN_REVIEW_VERDICT` (:345) and `\"review_ticket\": REVIEW_RESULT` (:350). The latter is currently the ONLY key keeping `review_result.schema.json` visible to the every-schema-file-is-wired guard, so it must be RE-POINTED (to the surviving `review-code`/workflow producer), not merely deleted, or the guard reports the schema orphaned.\n4. **MCP outputSchema coverage** — `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py:121` holds the `NO_SCHEMA_EXEMPT[\"review_ticket\"]` entry (the tool advertises no outputSchema); it must go with the tool or the coverage test fails on an unknown tool name.\n\n## Deprecation-registry treatment (mirrors the two prior pre-1.0 passes)\n\nDelete the three `_scheduled` rows at `src/rebar/_deprecations.py:128-130` plus their explanatory block comment at `:102-112`, and append this pass to the \"removed scheduled surfaces (historical record)\" NOTE block at `:131-141` — exactly the shape DE7 (`7e29166aec`) and the ticket-5899 sibling pass used. **NO tombstone**: the tombstone registry (`3eb3e71337`, postdating DE7) only accepts `env`/`cfg`/`file` kinds, and the precedent removals of CLI/lib/MCP surfaces (`list-epics`, `--no-sync`, the `list_epics` MCP tool, `rebar.list_epics()`) added none. Record \"operator-approved early removal (pre-1.0 pass #3), 2026-08-12\" in the historical NOTE.\n\n## Accepted risk\n\nThe survey flagged an **external importer of `rebar.llm.review_ticket`** as the one exposure that cannot be assessed from inside this repo. The operator approval covers it; announce-then-remove was already served by the v0.11.0 deprecation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] All three public surfaces are gone; checked: `rebar review x` exits non-zero as an unknown command, and `grep -rn \"review_ticket\" src/rebar/llm/__init__.py src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py` shows no public export or tool.\n- [ ] `_review_ticket_impl` still exists with its two live consumers intact; proven by `pytest tests/interfaces/store/test_review_as_workflow.py tests/unit/test_eval_solver.py`.\n- [ ] `review_result.schema.json` is still wired (not orphaned) and MCP outputSchema coverage passes; proven by `pytest tests/interfaces/facades/ tests/unit/test_output_schemas.py -q` and `pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py`.\n- [ ] Generated docs are REGENERATED, never hand-edited: `python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` and `python scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py`; checked: re-running them leaves the tree clean (`git diff --exit-code docs/cli-reference.md docs/mcp-reference.md`).\n- [ ] Hand-written docs no longer advertise the removed surfaces: `docs/llm-framework.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/output-schemas.md`, `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md`, `docs/llm-example-configs.md:94`, `README.md:175,230,241`. ADRs and the frozen eval corpus (`docs/experiments/**/*.jsonl`) are left as historical record.\n- [ ] The registry rows are deleted and the historical NOTE records the pass; checked: `pytest tests/unit/test_deprecation_registry.py`.\n- [ ] `docs/release-notes.md` and `CHANGELOG.md` carry a \"BREAKING (pre-1.0)\" entry in the prior passes' table format, worded so it does not read as a duplicate of the v0.11.0 \"retired the single-pass operation\" entry (`CHANGELOG.md:90,129`) — that one described the shim, this one describes the removal.\n- [ ] Gates green; checked: `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the full `pytest` suite.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` — the commit gate.\n- `pytest` (full suite) — 19 test files reference these surfaces; the shim suite `tests/unit/test_cli_review_alias.py` is deleted wholesale and the rest are retargeted to the surviving `review-plan`/engine paths.\n- `python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py && python scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py && git diff --exit-code docs/cli-reference.md docs/mcp-reference.md` — proves the generated docs match their sources (the CI drift gate).\n- `python scripts/check_server_manifest.py` — proves the `server.json` mirror of the MCP env description is back in sync.\n- `grep -rn \"review_ticket\\|rebar review \" src tests docs README.md` — raw grep, because string-named references (monkeypatch.setattr, MCP tool names, argv literals) are invisible to the LSP per `docs/code-navigation.md`.","id":"97d4-3098-2fb6-4658","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Remove the single-pass review public surfaces"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786567585488369001,"uuid":"b5b08bd7-1385-4f12-9e1f-dc435122fc2e"}